          "type": "text",
          "text": "**Defect — `parser.py:2`:** `bool(value)` checks truthiness, not valid Boolean strings. Consequently:\n- `\"false\"` incorrectly returns `True`.\n- `\"invalid\"` returns `True` and `\"\"` returns `False`, instead of raising `ValueError`.\n\n**Recommendation:** Explicitly accept only `\"true\"` → `True` and `\"false\"` → `False`; raise `ValueError` for everything else. Do not normalize case or whitespace.\n\nPrevent recurrence with regression tests covering both valid strings and rejected inputs: unknown strings, empty strings, uppercase variants, surrounding whitespace, and non-string values.\n\nNo files changed.",
